    <li><strong>Performance in the green zone:</strong> With 91 / 100 points, the home page loads quickly even on an average smartphone with a throttled mobile connection – just as Google simulates it in the test.</li>
    <li><strong>Full marks for SEO:</strong> 100 out of 100 points show that the page is technically clean and easily understood by search engines.</li>
    <li><strong>Accessible and reliable:</strong> 94 points for accessibility and 92 points for best practices ensure secure, modern access in your mobile browser.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What We Did to Speed Up Loading on Smartphones</h2>

  <p>
    The jump from 89 to 91 points is no accident – it is the result of targeted optimisations to the visible top of the page:
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>A leaner header image:</strong> The large banner at the top now uses the modern WebP format and is around a third smaller than before.</li>
    <li><strong>First things first:</strong> The browser loads the header image with top priority, before less important elements get their turn.</li>
    <li><strong>Notices without delay:</strong> The cookie notice now appears with the very first render instead of popping in afterwards.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Our goal remains for the mobile tools to feel just as weightless and immediate as they do on desktop – and we will keep working on it.
  </p>

